{
  "verses": [
    {
      "verse_num": 1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Make a joyful noise unto God, all ye lands:"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ all…: Heb. all the earth"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Sing forth the honour of his name: make his praise glorious."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Say unto God,"
        },
        {
          "type": "speech",
          "speaker": "Psalmist",
          "text": "How terrible art thou in thy works! through the greatness of thy power shall thine enemies submit themselves unto thee."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ submit…: or, yield feigned obedience: Heb. lie"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "speech",
          "speaker": "Psalmist",
          "text": "All the earth shall worship thee, and shall sing unto thee; they shall sing to thy name."
        },
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Selah."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Come and see the works of God: he is terrible in his doing toward the children of men."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He turned the sea into dry land: they went through the flood on foot: there did we rejoice in him."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He ruleth by his power for ever; his eyes behold the nations: let not the rebellious exalt themselves. Selah."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "O bless our God, ye people, and make the voice of his praise to be heard:"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Which holdeth our soul in life, and suffereth not our feet to be moved."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ holdeth: Heb. putteth"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "For thou, O God, hast proved us: thou hast tried us, as silver is tried."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Thou broughtest us into the net; thou laidst affliction upon our loins."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 12,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Thou hast caused men to ride over our heads; we went through fire and through water: but thou broughtest us out into a wealthy place."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ wealthy: Heb. moist"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 13,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "I will go into thy house with burnt offerings: I will pay thee my vows,"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 14,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Which my lips have uttered, and my mouth hath spoken, when I was in trouble."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ uttered: Heb. opened"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 15,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "I will offer unto thee burnt sacrifices of fatlings, with the incense of rams; I will offer bullocks with goats. Selah."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ fatlings: Heb. marrow"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 16,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Come and hear, all ye that fear God, and I will declare what he hath done for my soul."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 17,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "I cried unto him with my mouth, and he was extolled with my tongue."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 18,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "If I regard iniquity in my heart, the Lord will not hear me:"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 19,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "But verily God hath heard me; he hath attended to the voice of my prayer."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 20,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Blessed be God, which hath not turned away my prayer, nor his mercy from me."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    }
  ]
}